  {
    "episode_id": 90932,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90932.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's sort of a life philosophy that began from when I was a kid, you know, and my parents were teaching me about the values that they wanted me to live by. But the actual Wii before me title came from when I was in the Special Operations Unit that I was in, the Night Stalkers. And the nightstalkers at the time was still pretty classified. You couldn't talk about them. Black Hawk Down, the movie had come out. And these are the aviators who fly our Tier 1 assets, right? But they had a store where you could buy swag. And you just couldn't display this swag out in a real world. I bought a cap and sewn inside the cap were the words we before me. And I thought, wow, this is who I've always wanted to be. It's who my parents taught me to be. And of course, in an elite unit like that, you have to live that way. So I thought it was just a perfect title for the story of my life and the use of that philosophy to be successful.",
