    "turn_text": "Well, it's much about how you go about politics as opposed to what, because I mean, you have to fight for what you believe. That's the warrior part. And there are some lines I'm not going to cross. Everyone knows that I'm pro-second amendment, I'm pro-life, pro-family, small government. There are things that I'm not, I mean, I'm going to fight for those things. But what I'm not going to do is hate my friends who are on the other side of the aisle. I mean, they're Americans too. And we seem to have, and I think this is the whole social media thing. You know, it started with texting. My kids would text things that, you know, they'd be sitting in the backseat and they'd be texting one another instead of talking. And you would say things to people that you would never say face to face. And then social media amplified that. I mean, look at the posts, the things people say. You know, 20 years ago, we've never talked to one another like that. And then as that barrier in the conscience got brought down by doing this online, people are saying it face to face now. There's so much more of that. And so it's how not so much what. I mean, I I'm not going to change what I believe. That's the warrior part. But how I go about it, I want to bring our nation together. So let's find the areas where the Venn diagram overlaps and let's get that",
