  {
    "episode_id": 90932,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90932.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 93,
    "turn_text": "Well, it goes back to the idea of having that relationship first, right? So if in our Reagan O'Neill Club, I can actually sit down with Dean Phillips, who unfortunately isn't going to be in Congress after this cycle, but I could sit down with Dean and say, okay, let's argue this out. And Dean would say, this is why I believe what I believe. And I would say, well, this is why I believe what I believe. And sometimes I move him, sometimes he moves me, but you don't even have that opportunity. If you're standing there just yelling at each other, and so you have to have relationships first, then you can have a conversation. And maybe you can get to agreement on something. But if not, well then you have to come up with a third alternative.",
