    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90932.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 96,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, absolutely. So the trick is to, it's just like any sort of decision you have to make. You want to one, first, make sure the information you have is accurate. And oftentimes the information that is in social media and in the media, quite frankly, is not accurate. So you go back and make sure that your information is accurate. And then you get the emotion out of the way and you go have a conversation. It's a negotiation at that point. But if you're just knee-jerk response off what you see on social media, chances are you might be wrong. And I do my best. Despite the emotional upwelling that comes sometimes when I hear, oh, you know, we got to get rid of guns because that's what's, you know, I... I have to settle down and say, okay, what's driving that person? Let's go have a conversation. Let's show them the real data, the real numbers on this issue. And if they'll listen and not just knee jerk there, talking point or agenda item, then sure, we can have a conversation.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_08",
