    "turn_text": "now? Sure, you know, you gotta be fair. So I intend to, I intend to advance our agenda. I intend to advance President Trump's agenda, particularly as it relates to the areas of Homeland Security, right? The border, particularly the Southwest border, and obviously the cyber border, which is very, very much in my purview for CISA following in the homeland. And then the Secret Service, I mean, we've got a big overhaul to do there. Coast Guard, the Arctic, and Arctic, those are very big issues. So we've got a lot of things that are on our plate, but I will advance the agenda of this administration and of what we think the American people elected us to get done. Will they have an opportunity to provide input to that? Absolutely. You know, we had a, we were in the majority in the House when HR 2 went through. We had a Democrat and a Republican. Both attorneys, interestingly enough, Dan Bishop and Congressman Ivy from Maryland, both kind of two different positions. It's like 1 o'clock in the morning. I said, OK, you two, let's go to the back of the room. And so we go into the back of the room. I sit both of them down. I put a staffer at the computer and I'm like, let's work this out. All right, are you happy with that language or are you happy with that language? Let's amend the bill. We go back out and amend the bill and we all go home. So it's just being willing to make the sausage. I mean, nobody wants, you remember the old phrase, legislation is sausage making and it's not pretty, but you know, it's good on the other side. Well, you got to have actual leaders in the house willing to actually do that work. And I will admit, you know, when we first came into some of these confrontations, my staffers, you know, early on would say, no, just don't let them do it. Well, I mean, no, we're not going to do that. Move the bill to the bottom of the roster, let them work it out, and then we'll bring it back up. We're not just going to throw it out. So I think it takes that, doing that, being that kind of leader, Hopefully other people will join in.",
