    "turn_idx": 113,
    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, that's essentially what happened, right? I mean, we have 600,000 felons. 600,000 felons were allowed in under this administration. The interesting thing is most Democrats, the issue here isn't so much on my side because you can poll it, 70, 80% of Americans think that's a bad idea, right? Democrats have got to be honest and say, we're not going to support the old administration's policy because the old administration's policy is contrary to what the electorate wants. They're the ones that have to be honest on this one. I mean, I can say, do you want to let rapists and murderers in? There are 600,000 here now, you know, felons, not all rapists and murderers. And they have to be honest about that. I mean, it's their turn on this one. And if they say, you're right, that did happen, it shouldn't have happened. We want to be a part of the solution on that. We're going to bring them in. And I will tell you, they brought Bill's last cycle that we're really good and will be a part of our stuff we do this time around. Yes, not an issue of not listening, but we just have to be honest, go back to what are the real facts, the real facts. You can say a real fact, however impassioned you want to. You can't say something that is inaccurate.",
