  {
    "episode_id": 90932,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90932.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 123,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, because when you have relationships and you get to know one another and you can develop a mutual respect, even though you disagree, then you can have a conversation that can be substantive and maybe lead to something positive coming from it. But if you don't have the relationship, you know, you won't dial the rhetoric down. And so that's the whole point of let's have a relationship, let's have respect, and then let's have a conversation. And we're going to focus on this part of it and try to permeate that throughout. So it stops being, oh, all Democrats, all Republicans. And I've tried very hard to, in my tweets and in my posts, go, you know, this leader's doing that, or this person's doing that, and not all, you know, group everybody together. That's the rhetoric part that I don't like.",
