  {
    "episode_id": 90932,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90932.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 133,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I got the opportunity to introduce Senator McCain when he came to Tennessee back when he was running. And that guy, he's a war hero, right? I mean, do I agree with what he did on healthcare? One of the last things that he did as a United States Senator? No. And I thought that was... almost done with the wrong intentions. But I don't know that, so that's my perception, okay? But I will always say very positive things about John McCain because of the service to the country for his time in a POW camp that is just unimaginable, the challenge of that. And he overcame it, and so I'll have nothing but positive things to say about McCain.",
