    "turn_text": "Well, I'm fortunate enough to have had a lot of different experiences in life. So as a physician, as a business guy, military guy I can go into a community and there are for example there's a not-for-profit in downtown Nashville helping people start their you know African-American start their own business I can go in and look at what they're doing and say yeah this is the best way to teach a balanced statement or cash flow or whatever, right? Yeah, this is how you market. This is how you negotiate. And the particular one I'm speaking of, they're doing a phenomenal job, right? So you move on to the next one. Okay, how do we help these, right? Or healthcare, I can go to a free clinic, Matthew Walker clinic and go in and see what those guys are doing and say, you know, what about this? What about that? and then support them and make sure that they're getting the resources they need from, whether it's grants or helping them raise money as an offer profit, right? Because I ran an offer profit, actually, that did healthcare. So I bring that to the table. I think just being myself, you know, just, I love people. And if you really love the Wii, I mean, it doesn't matter. People are going to see that. If you're faking it, they're going to see that too. But I mean, I love everybody. And if you go show that, I mean, people warm up and they come and they talk to me. And I will say that there are people that have agendas, right? And it's hard to get around those individuals. And sometimes I've gone to particular groups and said, hey, I want to help. But that person had an agenda. and their agenda was to empower themselves, and they were living me before we. And so, wait a minute, I just had to go around that person. So, just be yourself, love people.",
