    "turn_text": "Yeah. Look, President Trump, people don't understand. They don't speak Trump, right? And that's the challenge. Go read Art of the Deal and you'll understand. When he says to the Mexican president, Amlow, we will put a 25% tariff if you do not start doing border security. That's sort of a shot across the bow. That's how he wins negotiations. He does deals that way. He kind of comes over here and then winds up getting what he needs. And of course, after that incident, they had Mexican military across the Guatemalan border, and Mexican military across the northern border stopping people from crossing. So, a lot of people, when he makes those statements, they don't understand. He's moving a needle, right? And this is his methodology. Now, in terms of rhetoric, look, we're going to advance an agenda. We're going to get as much cooperation as we can. And I, for one, am not going to be out there saying all Democrats are bad, all Democrat leaders are bad, you know, that sort of generalization rhetoric is what's getting us in trouble. What I will say as we contend with this issue is that problem, you attack the problem, not the person, that problem is wrong. We're not going to do that. So it's, again, it kind of gets back to how, and it's a subtle thing, but",
