    "turn_text": "I think it's for all of us, and I think I can share a story, and maybe this helps. AOC right after January 6 came out with a statement that said, all Republicans, I'm afraid of all Republicans. And I went to her on the floor of the house. She was sitting by herself a rare moment, sat down and said, you know, that really made me angry. That pissed me off because I'm a former soldier. If someone were threatening your life, I would have protected you. I would have. You know, the old sheepdog analogy. I'm a sheepdog and I would have protected you from anyone who was trying to hurt you. And she looks at me and says, and had actually a tear in her eyes, kind of puts her arm on my forearm and says, you're right, you would have and I shouldn't have said it that way. And I said, I tell you what, I'll promise to stop saying all Democrats. If you'll promise to stop saying all Republicans, and she said, yes, no, I don't know if she stuck to her promise, but I've tried to. Sometimes other people write our tweets and you got to catch the, no, don't say it that way, but let's attack the issue and not the",
