    "turn_text": "Well first my committee and then higher up. The only person I ever gabbled down in my committee was a Republican. The only words that I've ever had struck were of a Republican because they broke the rules. I have tried my best to be, and I've had Democrats come up and tell me you're the most fair chairman of all. And if I can just do that, Be fair, let people duke out their ideas, go in the back room, fix it, make it work. And be that guy, maybe we make a change overall. If others adopt that way. Now, going up. I think Mike Johnson, Speaker Johnson, is that kind of guy already. He's passionate about what he believes. He's going to support the agenda that the American people just spoke But he's not a confrontational guy where you're all bad and we're not listening to any of you. I think he'll go to the minority leader and work with him. And that'll happen many times. It's happened in his short tenure so far where we've actually passed bills that took both sides of the",
